  "worked_solution": "The function $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t}{{t}^{2}+4}$ is continuous on $[3,x],$ where $x>3.$ So, FTC II applies, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{3}^{x}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t}{{t}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{{x}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
